  "verbalization": "Tranilast is associated with Allergic Rhinitis through a chain of indications that involve Vasomotor Rhinitis. This pathway suggests that Tranilast may exert its effects on Vasomotor Rhinitis, which in turn could influence the development or severity of Allergic Rhinitis. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Tranilast is linked to Vasomotor Rhinitis via different agents—Mizolastine, Ramatroban, and Isoflupredone Acetate—each of which is indicated to treat Allergic Rhinitis. While the exact mechanism by which Tranilast affects Vasomotor Rhinitis remains unclear, the shared pathway from Tranilast to Vasomotor Rhinitis and then to Allergic Rhinitis suggests a potential role in the pathophysiology of allergic rhinitis. The integration of these paths highlights a possible mechanism where Tranilast may modulate inflammatory pathways or vascular responses, contributing to the development of allergic rhinitis.",
